From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 09:23:50 +0000
Subject: net: ethernet: lantiq: CBM port allocation and datapath glue

Add the CBM side of the datapath port contract:

 - cbm_dp.c: cbm_dp_port_alloc/dealloc (LAN datapath ports 2-5 map
   to TMU/dequeue port dp+5 and TMU queue dp+15, with the per-port
   DMA2TX channel handle), cbm_dp_enable (programs the QIDT
   queue-selection cube entry routing the port's endpoint to its
   TMU queue, or tears it down on disable, and - unless the probe
   already preconfigured it - sets up the DQM DMA egress port and
   its flat TMU egress path), and the resources_get export.

 - cbm_ports.c: the pmac/endpoint-to-egress-port registry
   (add/lookup/delete plus the endpoint-group lookup table
   assigning endpoints from the DT), and conf_dqm_cpu_port() - the
   vendor walk that configures the three CPU DQM rows (dequeue
   ports 2/1/3 with queues 35/34/36): reserve the ports, program
   the DQM CPU port and its flat TMU egress path, bind the
   endpoint from the DT, program the CPU QIDT rows to queue 35,
   and record the mapping in the registry. Queue 35 on dequeue
   port 2 is the host-RX path the RX engine drains.

Derived from the AVM FRITZ!Box 7560 GPL release (Linux 4.9.198),
cqm/grx500/cbm.c and cbm_config.c/h, which carry no copyright notice
of their own; the file headers name them as the origin.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

